# HomeNest Kitchen — environment configuration
# Copy to .env and adjust. SQLite keeps the zero-config local story:
#   npm install && npm run db:setup && npm run dev
# db:setup = `prisma db push` + seed (idempotent — safe to re-run).

# ---- Database -------------------------------------------------------------
# SQLite by default. The `db/` folder lives at the repo root (git-ignored).
# A RELATIVE `file:` URL is resolved against prisma/schema.prisma — exactly
# like the Prisma CLI — so `file:../db/custom.db` points at <repo>/db/custom.db
# for the CLI (push/seed), `next build`, and the running server alike,
# regardless of the process working directory. (src/lib/db-path.ts implements
# this resolution; tests/unit/db-path.test.ts pins the contract.)
# For production, an ABSOLUTE path is recommended.
DATABASE_URL="file:../db/custom.db"

# ---- Site ------------------------------------------------------------------
# Canonical public origin — used for metadata, sitemap.xml, and robots.txt.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=http://localhost:3000

# ---- Auth ------------------------------------------------------------------
# Session signing secret for the `homenest_session` cookie (HMAC).
# REQUIRED in production: the server REFUSES to start without a strong value
# (the insecure dev fallback throws at module load when NODE_ENV=production).
# Generate with: openssl rand -base64 32
AUTH_SECRET=""

# ---- Demo ------------------------------------------------------------------
# The login page ships a demo-credentials quick-fill box for development
# builds. In PRODUCTION builds the box is OFF by default (it names the seeded
# admin account) — set to "true" to opt back in for an evaluation deploy.
# Leave unset in development to show it; "false" hides it there too.
# Since session-13 the credentials are passed server-side as props only when
# enabled — a default production build ships no credential strings at all.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_DEMO_MODE=true

# ---- Rate limiting ---------------------------------------------------------
# clientIp (the per-IP limiter key) trusts Cloudflare's cf-connecting-ip by
# default. On a DIRECT deployment (no CF edge) that header is client-forgeable
# — set to "false" so it is ignored and the rightmost x-forwarded-for hop (or
# the shared "direct" bucket) is used instead.
# TRUST_CF_CONNECTING_IP="false"

# ---- Stripe payments (the Stripe retrofit, PAY-STRIPE-1) --------------------
# Empty by default: the checkout renders the demo card form (no charges) and
# PayPal/COD keep their manual/demo behavior. With real keys set, the card
# path becomes a real Stripe checkout: a Payment Element (PCI SAQ-A — card
# data never touches this app), a server-minted PaymentIntent (amount
# re-derived from the live cart + coupon + settings), and webhook-driven
# order placement for interrupted checkouts.
#   STRIPE_SECRET_KEY:                     sk_test_… (test mode) or sk_live_…
#   NEXT_PUBLIC_STRIPE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY:    pk_test_… / pk_live_…
#   STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET:                 whsec_… from `stripe listen` or the
#                                          dashboard endpoint for
#                                          POST /api/stripe/webhook
# See docs/DEPLOYMENT.md for the full setup (test cards, the local webhook
# listener, and the refund loop).
STRIPE_SECRET_KEY=""
NEXT_PUBLIC_STRIPE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=""
STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET=""
